  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Against his level, Owen's approach play is mixed. His greens in regulation are slightly above the Division I average, but his approach proximity is well behind it.\n\n- **Strokes gained approach:** He is at -4.16 strokes per round over his last 10 rounds. That window holds 8 rounds with stats, running 2026-06-09 to 2026-09-26. There is no college figure for strokes gained, so I can't compare him with his level on this metric. The team average is -3.09, and he is 6th of 7 players. The Tour baseline is 0.\n- **Greens in regulation:** He hit 61.11% over 144 holes in the same window. That is just above the Division I average of 60%, and he places 36th percent among college players over all recorded rounds. The team average is 62.76%, and he is 5th of 7. The Tour figure is 66%.\n- **Proximity from 125–175 yards:** His average is 50.58 ft over all recorded rounds. The Division I average is 38 ft, so he is 12.58 ft behind it, and he places 22nd percent among college players. The Tour figure is 30 ft. The team average for this stat wasn't available.\n\nHe finds greens at about the level average, but his shots finish farther from the hole than a typical college player's. That fits his negative strokes gained approach. His proximity from 125–175 yards is the first thing I'd look at.",
